{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/979378-help-me-decide-to-play-requiem-instead-of-masquerade","id":979378,"title":"Help me decide to play Requiem instead of Masquerade","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-30T18:09:43-07:00","id":979378,"title":"Help me decide to play Requiem instead of Masquerade","content":"So I realized while looking at house rules and such that I wanted for Masquerade, I was effectively making it more like Requiem, and since I like Requiem more and Masquerade primarily has nostalgia value, maybe I should just go ahead with Requiem.<br /> <br /> I am also somewhat reacting to Shane's comments about Chronicles of Darkness during the White Wolf Q&amp;A at Grand Masquerade.<br /> <br /> What makes Requiem cool?<br /> <br /> Stuff I like immediately is that there's explicit mechanical support for vampires as a group having enhanced senses, with Auspex covering more ESP-type stuff. This was what I was trying to adapt to Masquerade. I also like the smaller number of clans and the diverse covenants in contrast to the sects of Masquerade.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, I haven't played it yet so there's a lot of stuff I am probably missing. I mean my few things listed are minor.<br /> <br /> Also, which books work best with second edition?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T18:44:40-07:00","id":979402,"title":"","content":"You can't go wrong with the Clanbooks. They're very much the foundation for the Second Edition, and they add a wonderful, dark flavour to the world, as well as a palpable sense of history (whether you believe it or not).<br /> <br /> What attracts me to Requiem is its atmosphere. Vampires are parasites who play at politics and religion to keep themselves from devouring each other. Humanity is both your food and the one anchor that keeps you from falling into the maw of the Beast. You can be an aristocrat, a revolutionary, a witch, a mad scientist, a priest, or something else entirely, but at your core, you're a monster, and you have to figure out how to live with that. That's the Requiem. But as you grow older, as your blood thickens and your power grows, your challenge becomes not how to live with being a monster (there's no denying it anymore), but what the best monster you can be is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T18:53:45-07:00","id":979407,"title":"","content":"In my opinion, Requiem - and Requiem 2e in particular - does an incredible job of showing the descent into monstrosity. Losing Humanity makes you take more damage from Sunlight, and makes your Clan Bane (along with any additional Banes you've gained) get worse. Humanity is lost not by committing sins, but by experiencing things that distance you from the human experience. You can protect your humanity to a limited degree by maintaining personal relationships with humans who remind you of what it felt like to be human yourself.<br /> <br /> I also love the background and worldbuilding details of Requiem. Without having a metaplot (which I personally find intrusive), it manages to have a rich history and background details, and still leaves a lot of space for the ST to fill in. Like, to use video games as an analogy, if Masquerade was a BioWare game, and Requiem would be a From Software game.<br /> <br /> The local scale is a plus for me. I generally like personal stories more than epics.<br /> <br /> As for what 1e books work best with 2e, definitely get Damnation City. That might be the best resource in all of 1e's run, and most of it can be ported to 2e with little to no legwork. The Clan books are also fantastic, they're 90% story material, all told through in-character doccuments, with rules appendicies at the end. Not all of the rules can be easily ported to 2e, but some of them can, and the others are worth the extra work (or you could use one of the fan conversions you can find in the homebrew hub). But really, you want the Clan books for their fluff anyway. They paint a fantastic picture of the Clans' identities, their place in the setting, and they were some of the first hints of setting details that would continue to get fleshed out across 1e's run, and at this point are regarded as more-or-less canon in 2e, including the Clans' origins and the existence of the Strix. I would recommend the Covenant books as well to get a more in-depth look at the Covenants than the core book gives, but the Covenant identities got a bit of a facelift for 2e so it wouldn't all be relevant, and besides, Secrets of the Covenants might be coming out soon (fingers crossed), and it's going to be written in the same style as the Clan books, which has got me excited. Blood Sorcery: Sacraments and Blasphemies is also worth a look. It significantly expands the blood sorcery Disciplines, in a way that is fully comparable with 2e (in fact, 2e's revisions to blood sorcery were based on the system in that book).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T19:17:49-07:00","id":979421,"title":"","content":"If you like the diverse covenants, it is worth noting that the five core covenants are just the ones most common in the modern western kindred domains, the sample settings in 2e include multiple examples of other covenants in domains around the world, including the very interesting set up in Tokyo (2e's official crossover sample setting), where the Lancea et Sanctum is the only one of the usual covenants present and one of the local factions the kindred can join is lead by a group of human corporate executives holding the masquerade hostage as part of a plan to conquer the supernaturals of Japan.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T20:24:56-07:00","id":979451,"title":"","content":"Okay, so clanbooks, Damnation City, and Blood Sorcery. Excellent.<br /> <br /> I love the banes way more than the previous clan weaknesses. They make things more interesting, at least from reading.<br /> <br /> I really need to finish reading the sample settings. I set the book aside awhile back while I was still reading about the Strix.<br /> <br /> I love the From Software comparison. I love Dark Souls.<br /> <br /> I really like how humanity looks to work in Requiem - it's an interesting take as compared to the previous morality.<br /> <br /> Thanks much. Not that I was a hard sell. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T20:53:17-07:00","id":979463,"title":"","content":"The big thing for me is that there's more story potential in five uneasy Covenants than there ever was in open Jyhad between two Sects; while the Sabbat were your monstrous vampires and your Camarilla were your ostensibly humane vampires, there was no time to debate that because you had kill-on-sight orders or huge swathes of territory apart from each other. I love that Requiem lets each and every member of your coterie be pulled apart by factionalism and ideology, but you still have to play nice because these assholes are the only thing keeping you safe from everyone else.<br /> <br /> The biggest shift in going from Masquerade to Requiem is probably in clans going from distinct lineages to loose archetypes, but that's incredibly freeing to me. Whereas &quot;I'm a Ravnos&quot; was the core of your Masquerade character, all a Requiem clan gives you is means to be and do whatever you want; there are Bloodlines if you want to fit into something larger, but by default your character stands alone rather than defined by a dozen generations of context and stereotypes. That they're also more flexible (Nosferatu that aren't physically hideous, but still somehow off and disquieting!) and less racist (Bye-bye, Assamites amd all the baggage that comes with belief-driven Middle Eastern killers!) is just gravy on top for me.<br /> <br /> Other than that, the cleaner nWoD/CofD rules are a boon and so is not having to race alongside a metaplot or know a mountain of canon characters. The best book by far is Danse Macabre and while a lot of the optional rules in that have been folded into 2e by default (though not the brilliant Atrocity Dice, which I hope have a place in Hunter) there's some amazing advice on what makes Requiem tick and how to make it your game. Requiem For Rome is a blast if you're a history nerd like me and it nails the cinemativ feel of bloody, decadent, globe-spanning Rome. VII gives three contradictory truths behind the shadowy antagonist group that haunted 1e and all of them are brilliant, but special love goes out to Stolze's take in a lost demon-haunted clan that hates the Kindred. Ancient Bloodlines/Ancient Mysteries are great for showing the crazy setting diversity that Requiem allows, the clanbooks all come highly praised by Mekhet is the only one I read (and adored), and then the Night Horrors books are disgustingly great.<br /> <br /> Welcome to the other Vampire game! If you're like me, you'll never go back.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T09:27:30-07:00","id":979717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/979378-help-me-decide-to-play-requiem-instead-of-masquerade?p=979407#post979407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The Clan books are also fantastic, they're 90% story material, all told through in-character doccuments, with rules appendicies at the end. Not all of the rules can be easily ported to 2e, but some of them can, and the others are worth the extra work (or you could use one of the fan conversions you can find in the homebrew hub).</div> </div> </div> </div>I think a lot of the additional rules in the clan books already got ported directly into VtR2. There are lots of merits and some rules bits that were shown in the clan books for the first time, and were moved to the core book for 2e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1681-murder-of-crows","name":"Murder-of-Crows","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1681_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T09:43:20-07:00","id":979731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murder-of-Crows</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/979378-help-me-decide-to-play-requiem-instead-of-masquerade?p=979717#post979717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think a lot of the additional rules in the clan books already got ported directly into VtR2. There are lots of merits and some rules bits that were shown in the clan books for the first time, and were moved to the core book for 2e.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lots of them did, yeah. Lots of them also didn't, like Malkavia, Hollow Mekhet, and the Red Surrender, Of Rose and Thorn, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T09:50:56-07:00","id":979735,"title":"","content":"I think M is mentioned in the core rulebook (that is Malkavia, right?) but it's not detailed to any degree.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T10:46:36-07:00","id":979753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/979378-help-me-decide-to-play-requiem-instead-of-masquerade?p=979735#post979735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think M is mentioned in the core rulebook (that is Malkavia, right?) but it's not detailed to any degree.</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically, it's Requiem's take on Malkavians, as a contagious illness rather than a Clan. Malkav was the first Kindred diagnosed with it, and was a Ventrue, so although it can affect any Kindred, the stereotype is that it's a Ventrue disease, much like the &quot;AIDS is a gay disease&quot; stereotype. It's further detailed in the Ventrue Clan book, and is one of the most commonly fan-adapted mechanics from 1e to 2e. Shameless plug, I did a version of it that was meant to replicate the mechanics of the disease from the Clan book as closely as possible within the 2e rules. I think I could have done the Bloodline Gifts better, and in retrospect I'm not sure I would give them Nightmare as a 4th discipline, but I'm rather proud of my conversion of the disease mechanics and the writeup overall.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T11:44:21-07:00","id":979774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/979378-help-me-decide-to-play-requiem-instead-of-masquerade?p=979753#post979753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Basically, it's Requiem's take on Malkavians, as a contagious illness rather than a Clan. Malkav was the first Kindred diagnosed with it, and was a Ventrue, so although it can affect any Kindred, the stereotype is that it's a Ventrue disease, much like the &quot;AIDS is a gay disease&quot; stereotype. It's further detailed in the Ventrue Clan book, and is one of the most commonly fan-adapted mechanics from 1e to 2e. Shameless plug, I did a version of it that was meant to replicate the mechanics of the disease from the Clan book as closely as possible within the 2e rules. I think I could have done the Bloodline Gifts better, and in retrospect I'm not sure I would give them Nightmare as a 4th discipline, but I'm rather proud of my conversion of the disease mechanics and the writeup overall.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ooh do you have a link to your version?<br /> <br /> I've read at least one other conversion, but I forgot who wrote it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T11:53:45-07:00","id":979781,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hNssb3w0QxV6sTEs66qpd1uN49o3L7GS7Hh7zL2os58/mobilebasic\" target=\"_blank\">Indeed, I do.</a><br /> <br /> If I had the time, I would probably re-work the Bloodline Gifts to give them some more oomph and drop the 4th Discipline. But the fluff is solid, as is the disease mechanics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T13:50:13-07:00","id":979833,"title":"","content":"Just my 2 cents. <br /> Requiem mechanically smoothed vampire to a much more playable system. <br /> <br /> It's easier to change the names of the players in metaplot than rebuild the wheel, if nostalgia is tugging at your brain <br /> <br /> 2e is even better imo. Added lots of neat fiddly bits to play with. Also made vampires feel more like classic monsters than school yard bullies 1e left them feeling like. And don't neglect the storyteller section in 2e, lots of great toys to make the feel of the game really immersive.<br /> <br /> Charlaquin nailed the books dead on, but if budget is an issue maybe wait for secrets of the covenants. <br /> Oh and one of my personal favorites The Blood. More for setting the feel.<br /> <br /> If you are still conflicted maybe try a one shot type game in each system and see which is more your taste. Cuz sometimes you just have to say system be damned, this feels more like what I want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1117-overload","name":"overload","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1117_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T14:23:47-07:00","id":979854,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar269_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"269\" data-vbnamecard=\"269\">Charlaquin</a> Thank you, that's good stuff. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I appreciate all the advice and commentary posted in this thread. I'm definitely going to be running a Requiem game in the near future (probably in November, but hopefully in October), and I am going to convert my first ever Vampire chronicle / city to Requiem (also moving everything to a different city). So far the hardest decision I have to make is what clan to make my formerly Brujah prince. It's a tossup between Ventrue and Gangrel.<br /> <br /> What I like about Requiem is that it reminds me of that first game I ran, and brings the emphasis back to the <i>personal</i> that Masquerade advertises (A Storytelling Game of Personal Horror) and I mean don't get me wrong - I still love Masquerade but Requiem feels like those early games to me in a way that Masquerade doesn't.<br /> <br /> Now I just need to finish populating the city, as it needs about 10x more vampires. Well, not &quot;finish,&quot; but flesh things out at least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T15:21:41-07:00","id":979887,"title":"","content":"Why not just make your Brujah prince Deva? The clans are flexible enough in Requiem that going against stereotype is easy and fun. Deva don't have to be the seducer. I only say this because they share the same initial discipline spread. Not sure if that matters.<br /> <br /> Also, I would strongly recommend the covenant books. Especially the Invictus book because its a great insight into vampire high society. It gives a lot of neat ideas on how to set up the prince's court (if they happen to be Invictus).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8306-wissenschaft","name":"Wissenschaft","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T15:31:22-07:00","id":979891,"title":"","content":"Daeva wouldn't fit or that would have been my first choice <i>because</i> of the discipline spread. So the choice to go Ventrue or Gangrel comes down to which aspect of the character I want to emphasize. Not that clan defines a person but it's kinda relevant.<br /> <br /> And I have quite a list of books ahead of me. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T15:48:58-07:00","id":979896,"title":"","content":"My Masquerade knowledge is limited, but as I understand it, Brujah are hot-headed and rebelious, yeah? Deva are defined by passion, and hot-headed and rebellious is a perfectly valid expression of passion. What are the traits of this character that push you towards Ventrue and Gangrel?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T15:52:55-07:00","id":979897,"title":"","content":"If I were to sum up the requiem clan's identities in one word each, they would be<br /> <br /> Deva: Passion<br /> Gangrel: Instinct<br /> Mekhet: Knowledge<br /> Nosferatu: Fear<br /> Ventrue: Power","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T16:09:22-07:00","id":979902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/979378-help-me-decide-to-play-requiem-instead-of-masquerade#post979378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I realized while looking at house rules and such that I wanted for Masquerade, I was effectively making it more like Requiem, and since I like Requiem more and Masquerade primarily has nostalgia value, maybe I should just go ahead with Requiem.<br /> <br /> I am also somewhat reacting to Shane's comments about Chronicles of Darkness during the White Wolf Q&amp;A at Grand Masquerade.<br /> <br /> What makes Requiem cool?<br /> <br /> Stuff I like immediately is that there's explicit mechanical support for vampires as a group having enhanced senses, with Auspex covering more ESP-type stuff. This was what I was trying to adapt to Masquerade. I also like the smaller number of clans and the diverse covenants in contrast to the sects of Masquerade.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, I haven't played it yet so there's a lot of stuff I am probably missing. I mean my few things listed are minor.<br /> <br /> Also, which books work best with second edition?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> For one thing, there's no progenitor myth and no generations curse. Your vampire's power levels increases with age and experience, and likewise decreases from long periods of torpor. Generally 50 years in torpor decreases blood potency by 1 point.<br /> <br /> This means that Kindred society in requiem is equal opportunity. The most powerful vampires are the ones who stay active, while those who attempt to sleep through the ages suffer a decrease in their capabilities. If the Antedeluvians tried to pull a doomsday stunt in Requiem, they'd find themselves as weak as Fledglings after sleeping for a few thousand years. And it would probably take centuries for them to even recover an ounce of their lost power.<br /> <br /> <br /> Another thing to like is that the occult affiliated vampires (Tremere, Setites, Baali, est) can now be converted into factions in which any vampire can join, instead of being an exclusive clan. Blood Magic, Necromancy, Serpentis, Daimoinon, they're free for all to enjoy... as long as you sign on with the right covenant...<br /> <br /> <br /> Ultimately, this means that such vampires can come from wider backgrounds than the stereotypical counterparts from Masquerade. Giving you more creative freedom for designing such a character.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 10-01-2016, 07:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T16:11:39-07:00","id":979907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/979378-help-me-decide-to-play-requiem-instead-of-masquerade?p=979896#post979896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My Masquerade knowledge is limited, but as I understand it, Brujah are hot-headed and rebelious, yeah? Deva are defined by passion, and hot-headed and rebellious is a perfectly valid expression of passion. What are the traits of this character that push you towards Ventrue and Gangrel?</div> </div> </div> </div>For Ventrue:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> See the big boss. Meeting the man himself is a tedious ritual. You have to know a guy who knows a guy. You have to get pastgoon after goon. There is a hidden smoke-filled room, past several other smoke-filled rooms, a nasty nesting doll of power. There he is. Broad shoulders form a power-house V in that pinstripe power suit. You tremble as you step forward, kiss his emerald ring. He is the apex and the fulcrum. All the city is his pendulum. City aldermen, criminals, Christ\u2026everyone spends time in his pocket. He flushes red as he talks, and you shiver. In awe, you barely notice the little old woman, sitting as still as death in the corner\u2014 the one he looks to before giving every opinion and answer. </div> </div> </div><br /> For Gangrel:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> See the CEO. They say successful businessmen have personality traits in common with sociopaths and predators. He\u2019s Shere Khan in a three-piece suit. The rules really didn\u2019t change. Eat or be eaten. Greed is good. The skyscraper is just another jungle, and he claimed it, floor to floor, marking with his own blood. He knows everything that goes on in his jungle. Every jackal and leopard bows to him. How they yowl, growl, and howl. Sometimes the primal metaphors cut too literal. He messes up so many suits. But he just sloughs them off like a molting animal. In his penthouse apartment, there is a closet with rows of suits like rotating shark teeth. </div> </div> </div>Like not literally these paragraphs from the clan writeups, but that's sort of the general feeling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T16:17:00-07:00","id":979912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/979378-help-me-decide-to-play-requiem-instead-of-masquerade?p=979902#post979902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For one thing, there's no progenitor myth and no generations curse. Your vampire's power levels increases with age and experience, and likewise decreases from long periods of torpor. Generally 50 years in torpor decreases blood potency by 1 point.<br /> <br /> This means that Kindred society in requiem is equal opportunity. The most powerful vampires are the ones who stay active, while those who attempt to sleep through the ages suffer a decrease in their capabilities. If the Antedeluvians tried to pull a doomsday stunt in Requiem, they'd find themselves as weak as Fledglings after sleeping for a few thousand years. And it would probably take centuries for them to even recover an ounce of their lost power.</div> </div> </div> </div>In Requiem 2e they don't lose dots though? I know in 1e they lost dots when their new maximum was lower than some of their traits, but in 2e they keep the traits? Their blood potency is still pretty weak, though, so yeah.<br /> <br /> I love blood potency over generation, as well as the lack of a progenitor myth and the sense that each of the clans has its own unique origin.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Another thing to like is that the occult affiliated vampires (Tremere, Setites, Baali, est) can now be converted into factions in which any vampire can join, instead of being an exclusive clan. Blood Magic, Necromancy, Serpentis, Daimoinon, they're free for all to enjoy... as long as you sign on with the right covenant...<br /> <br /> Ultimately, this means that such vampires can come from wider backgrounds than the stereotypical counterparts from Masquerade. Giving you more creative freedom for designing such a character. </div> </div> </div>This is genuinely great. The Tremere in my old city are getting split into different clans and divided between the Circle of the Crone and Ordo Dracul. I have different ideas for Lancea et Sanctum, though.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T16:22:21-07:00","id":979916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/979378-help-me-decide-to-play-requiem-instead-of-masquerade?p=979912#post979912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In Requiem 2e they don't lose dots though? I know in 1e they lost dots when their new maximum was lower than some of their traits, but in 2e they keep the traits? Their blood potency is still pretty weak, though, so yeah.<br /> <br /> I love blood potency over generation, as well as the lack of a progenitor myth and the sense that each of the clans has its own unique origin.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> They don't lose dots, per se, they just lose access to those dots until their blood potency returned to the appropriate level. It was basically pre-purchased traits that became unlocked as you regained your lost power. Blood Potency sort of measures the cap you can have on such traits. From 1-5 you have the standard 5 dot cap on your abilities. But but once you hit 6 and onward, you can push yourself beyond normal human limits.<br /> <br /> In Masquerade, your maximum traits were determined by how high or low your Generation is. But in Masquerade, you could only change that through Diablerie. In Requiem, you can reach the next level without having to commit Amaranth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 10-01-2016, 07:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T16:25:29-07:00","id":979919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/979378-help-me-decide-to-play-requiem-instead-of-masquerade?p=979912#post979912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In Requiem 2e they don't lose dots though? I know in 1e they lost dots when their new maximum was lower than some of their traits, but in 2e they keep the traits? Their blood potency is still pretty weak, though, so yeah.<br /> <br /> I love blood potency over generation, as well as the lack of a progenitor myth and the sense that each of the clans has its own unique origin.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, right. In 2ed the dots over 5 stills even if BP get lower.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T16:26:56-07:00","id":979920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/979378-help-me-decide-to-play-requiem-instead-of-masquerade?p=979897#post979897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I were to sum up the requiem clan's identities in one word each, they would be<br /> <br /> Deva: Passion<br /> Gangrel: Instinct<br /> Mekhet: Knowledge<br /> Nosferatu: Fear<br /> Ventrue: Power</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> In fact, Requiem 2nd edition slightly differentiates each clan's beast. A Venture's beast is driven to dominate/control others while a Deva's beast drives them to seduce/manipulate others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8306-wissenschaft","name":"Wissenschaft","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T16:27:54-07:00","id":979921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/979378-help-me-decide-to-play-requiem-instead-of-masquerade?p=979916#post979916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> They don't lose dots, per se, they just lose access to those dots until their blood potency returned to the appropriate level. It was basically pre-purchased traits that became unlocked as you regained your lost power. Blood Potency measures the cap you can have on such traits. 1-5 is the normal 5 cap. But from 6 to 10, the cap increases beyond human limits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, okay. Makes sense.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T16:29:01-07:00","id":979922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/979378-help-me-decide-to-play-requiem-instead-of-masquerade?p=979916#post979916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> They don't lose dots, per se, they just lose access to those dots until their blood potency returned to the appropriate level.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you sure? Where is it written?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T16:31:22-07:00","id":979924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/979378-help-me-decide-to-play-requiem-instead-of-masquerade?p=979922#post979922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Are you sure? Where is it written?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Should be under the effects of Torpor. Doesn't it mention their extra dots being <i>temporarily</i> lost until their blood potency is restored? Or did I misinterpret their meaning?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T16:39:26-07:00","id":979930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/979378-help-me-decide-to-play-requiem-instead-of-masquerade?p=979924#post979924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Should be under the effects of Torpor. Doesn't it mention their extra dots being <i>temporarily</i> lost until their blood potency is restored? Or did I misinterpret their meaning?</div> </div> </div> </div>I will check it again but I think that there isn't this specification. I let you know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T16:49:15-07:00","id":979933,"title":"","content":"the book simply says:&quot;When her Blood Potency falls below six dots, the vampire does not lose any Attributes or Skills above the fifth dot.&quot;. So I think she never lose the use of her dots above 5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 10-01-2016, 07:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T16:54:43-07:00","id":979935,"title":"","content":"Oh oh I have a question:<br /> <br /> There is no such thing as Disciplines at 6+ dots, yes? Only Devotions as a way to expand one's use of Disciplines?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T17:01:01-07:00","id":979939,"title":"","content":"No. Disciplines are just until 5th dot. But a 5 dot in 2ed is at the same level of a 7-8 dot of Masquerade counterpart and even more powerful than the 5 dot of requiem 1ed. With Devotion you can trascend even the 5 dot power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 10-01-2016, 08:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T17:02:36-07:00","id":979940,"title":"","content":"One advantage Requiem has over Masquerade is the lack of a metaplot. It's a toolkit and a sandbox where you can tell the stories you want to tell, not the story that White Wolf is telling you. So there's zero chance of having your game railroaded by metaplot. While I do not like the emphasis of the Strix in 2e (among other changes made, mostly mechanical), even that is entirely optional in Requiem. My games do hot have Strix, but you do have that option. Nothing is set in stone and that is wonderful, at least in my opinion.<br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T17:16:48-07:00","id":979946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/979378-help-me-decide-to-play-requiem-instead-of-masquerade?p=979935#post979935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh oh I have a question:<br /> <br /> There is no such thing as Disciplines at 6+ dots, yes? Only Devotions as a way to expand one's use of Disciplines?</div> </div> </div> </div>Correct. 1st edition played with the idea of 6+ dot Disciplines a little, but didn't do much with it, and 2e just decided to kill it and make Devotions the primary way of expanding Disciplines. They're not necessarily the only way, though. There are Merits that expand on Disciplines too, Blood Sorcery (technically 1e, but kind of an honorary 2e book) had something called Threnodies. There's always the possibility of Thousand Years of Night giving more expansion options for high-level characters as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T17:24:36-07:00","id":979951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/979378-help-me-decide-to-play-requiem-instead-of-masquerade?p=979933#post979933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the book simply says:&quot;When her Blood Potency falls below six dots, the vampire does not lose any Attributes or Skills above the fifth dot.&quot;. So I think she never lose the use of her dots above 5.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh... Well then... forget the part about equal opportunity.<br /> <br /> <br /> Oh, no wait, now I remember!<br /> <br /> <i>You couldn't advance your traits further</i> until your blood potency reached the appropriate level.<br /> <br /> So yeah, I guess the elders would still be the ones in check after waking up. Depending on how long they slept, giving neonates time to rival them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T17:39:37-07:00","id":979958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/979378-help-me-decide-to-play-requiem-instead-of-masquerade?p=979940#post979940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One advantage Requiem has over Masquerade is the lack of a metaplot. It's a toolkit and a sandbox where you can tell the stories you want to tell, not the story that White Wolf is telling you. So there's zero chance of having your game railroaded by metaplot. While I do not like the emphasis of the Strix in 2e (among other changes made, mostly mechanical), even that is entirely optional in Requiem. My games do hot have Strix, but you do have that option. Nothing is set in stone and that is wonderful, at least in my opinion.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was gonna go with the relatively metaplot neutral V20, but yeah. I like the sandboxiness of Requiem.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/979378-help-me-decide-to-play-requiem-instead-of-masquerade?p=979946#post979946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Correct. 1st edition played with the idea of 6+ dot Disciplines a little, but didn't do much with it, and 2e just decided to kill it and make Devotions the primary way of expanding Disciplines. They're not necessarily the only way, though. There are Merits that expand on Disciplines too, Blood Sorcery (technically 1e, but kind of an honorary 2e book) had something called Threnodies. There's always the possibility of Thousand Years of Night giving more expansion options for high-level characters as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm really looking forward to Thousand Years of Night.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/979378-help-me-decide-to-play-requiem-instead-of-masquerade?p=979951#post979951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh... Well then... forget the part about equal opportunity.<br /> <br /> Oh, no wait, now I remember!<br /> <br /> <i>You couldn't advance your traits further</i> until your blood potency reached the appropriate level.<br /> <br /> So yeah, I guess the elders would still be the ones in check after waking up. Depending on how long they slept, giving neonates time to rival them.</div> </div> </div> </div>An elder with sufficiently high traits and enough Disciplines seems like they can still be pretty scary, but their low BP will certainly limit that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T19:12:45-07:00","id":980001,"title":"","content":"I don't think vampires lose those 6+ attributes, skills and disciplines anymore if their blood potency drops.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 10-01-2016, 10:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T20:04:56-07:00","id":980025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/979378-help-me-decide-to-play-requiem-instead-of-masquerade?p=980001#post980001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think vampires lose those 6+ attributes, skills and disciplines anymore if their blood potency drops.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, seems like I remembered it wrong.<br /> <br /> It actually says they can't advance their abilities further until their BP reaches the appropriate level again.<br /> <br /> So in other words, a vampire can go to sleep with 7 Strength, drop their BP down to 4, and wake up again with 7 Strength, but can't increase it to 8 until their BP reaches the same level.<br /> <br /> <br /> So, depending on how long the elder / ancient was asleep for, the former neonates could rise up to challenge their power, and it would take a long time for the revived elder to start improving their abilities to the point where they regain control.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/979378-help-me-decide-to-play-requiem-instead-of-masquerade?p=979891#post979891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Daeva wouldn't fit or that would have been my first choice <i>because</i> of the discipline spread. So the choice to go Ventrue or Gangrel comes down to which aspect of the character I want to emphasize. Not that clan defines a person but it's kinda relevant.<br /> <br /> And I have quite a list of books ahead of me. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh, yeah, another cool thing about Requiem is that bloodlines can apparently come from two or more clans forming an intimate alliance. The Giovanni clan, for example, is now the Sangiovanni family, which is a hybrid bloodline of Mekhet and Ventrue working together.<br /> <br /> <b>NOTE:</b> Some wikis describe the Sangiovanni as Ventrue, and others as Mekhet, but they're apparently both.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 10-01-2016, 11:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T05:26:02-07:00","id":980198,"title":"","content":"That depends on the scenario, the elder who went into torpor and jacked up their key attributes, skills, and disciplines to 7 or 8 before entering torpor last time, is going to have a much easier time reconsolidating power and amassing influence than the 20 years dead neonate who has to split their attention developing everything. The only thing that may or may not offset that elder is the comparative power of enemies he likely accumulated last time he was active.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T11:37:09-07:00","id":980357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/979378-help-me-decide-to-play-requiem-instead-of-masquerade?p=980025#post980025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, yeah, another cool thing about Requiem is that bloodlines can apparently come from two or more clans forming an intimate alliance. The Giovanni clan, for example, is now the Sangiovanni family, which is a hybrid bloodline of Mekhet and Ventrue working together.<br /> <br /> <b>NOTE:</b> Some wikis describe the Sangiovanni as Ventrue, and others as Mekhet, but they're apparently both.</div> </div> </div> </div>Per 1E core and Bloodlines: the Chosen the Sangiovanni are solely a Mekhet bloodline. Unless there's other published material on them somewhere (which I don't believe there is), any Ventrue connection is non-canon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T11:49:14-07:00","id":980362,"title":"","content":"It is true though that there are some Bloodlines accessible to multiple Clans. Moroi can be Gangrel or Nosferatu. Lincii can be Nosferatu or Julii. I don't think it's ever explicitly stated, but it's strongly hinted that Macellarius can be Julii or Ventrue. In all cases, the Bloodline is described as an anomaly, as one Bloodline with multiple parent Clans shouldn't be possible. Their &quot;true&quot; origins are always a matter of mystery and controversy. Then there's the Neglatu, which are a Revenant Bloodline and can be of any Clan. With them it's less a question of which Clan is their true parent, and more a question of which came first - the Neglatu or the Kindred.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T12:08:09-07:00","id":980372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/979378-help-me-decide-to-play-requiem-instead-of-masquerade?p=980357#post980357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Per 1E core and Bloodlines: the Chosen the Sangiovanni are solely a Mekhet bloodline. Unless there's other published material on them somewhere (which I don't believe there is), any Ventrue connection is non-canon.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't know about published, but I first came across the idea while looking up a list of bloodlines for Requiem (I believe the original site no longer exists, unfortunately). In addition to the Sangiovanni, other versions of the 13 clans were remade into bloodlines.<br /> <br /> Tzimisce were turned into a Ventrue bloodline, for example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T12:30:00-07:00","id":980380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/979378-help-me-decide-to-play-requiem-instead-of-masquerade?p=980372#post980372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know about published, but I first came across the idea while looking up a list of bloodlines for Requiem (I believe the original site no longer exists, unfortunately). In addition to the Sangiovanni, other versions of the 13 clans were remade into bloodlines.<br /> <br /> Tzimisce were turned into a Ventrue bloodline, for example.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like fan conversions, or maybe the translation guide. Oh, speaking of which, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2367_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2367\" data-vbnamecard=\"2367\">Resplendent Fire</a>, another good 1e book to add to your reading list since you're a big Masquerade fan might be the Vampire Translation Guide. It's a book full of advice for converting elements of Masquerade to Requiem and of Requiem to Masquerade. It's based on 1e Requiem's and V20's systems, but it could be a good source of inspiration, if you've got any favorite Masquerade elements you'd like to add to your Requiem toolbox.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T15:20:17-07:00","id":980444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/979378-help-me-decide-to-play-requiem-instead-of-masquerade?p=980380#post980380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sounds like fan conversions, or maybe the translation guide. Oh, speaking of which, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2367_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2367\" data-vbnamecard=\"2367\">Resplendent Fire</a>, another good 1e book to add to your reading list since you're a big Masquerade fan might be the Vampire Translation Guide. It's a book full of advice for converting elements of Masquerade to Requiem and of Requiem to Masquerade. It's based on 1e Requiem's and V20's systems, but it could be a good source of inspiration, if you've got any favorite Masquerade elements you'd like to add to your Requiem toolbox.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for pointing this out. Definitely worth !looking into.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T02:22:18-07:00","id":981359,"title":"","content":"I just have two corrections to make:<br /> It's Daeva not deva;<br /> And Disciplines are capped at 5 .Even if you reach BP 10, you can only increase your attributes and skills above 5 (however such a vampire is likely to have numerous devotions)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T13:23:48-07:00","id":981655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/979378-help-me-decide-to-play-requiem-instead-of-masquerade?p=981359#post981359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just have two corrections to make:<br /> It's Daeva not deva</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I was pretty sure I was spelling it wrong when I wrote Deva, but I was having one of those moments where a word just doesn't look right even when you spell it correctly (other people get those moments too, right? It's not just me?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T14:19:46-07:00","id":981691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/979378-help-me-decide-to-play-requiem-instead-of-masquerade?p=981655#post981655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I was pretty sure I was spelling it wrong when I wrote Deva, but I was having one of those moments where a word just doesn't look right even when you spell it correctly (other people get those moments too, right? It's not just me?)</div> </div> </div> </div>Not just you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T14:49:06-07:00","id":981704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/979378-help-me-decide-to-play-requiem-instead-of-masquerade?p=981655#post981655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I was pretty sure I was spelling it wrong when I wrote Deva, but I was having one of those moments where a word just doesn't look right even when you spell it correctly (other people get those moments too, right? It's not just me?)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I can confirm that those moments do happen for other people (at least for me). It's a fucked up feeling where my brain (suspect yours too) just refuses to accept a word. And then the more you think about the word the more fucked up it seems <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T16:44:52-07:00","id":981791,"title":"","content":"If your concidering Tokyo, you might benifit from Changeling the lost 2e, you actually learn about the wider domains in Honsu abit, not just Tokyo, as well as a couple of Changelings who are very involved in Vampire politics. One is the Changelings Ambassador/Envoy to Vampires, an interesting Character, the other is an Ambassador/Envoy to humanity, including a human lead Corporation that is a major power in Tokyo Vampire politics.<br /> <br /> But one thing I would do is add some Jiang Shi to Osaka, just because I find the Jiang Shi interesting, why leave out a interesting, if rare clan.<br /> <br /> I think CoD 2e does have a metaplot, but its mostly unique regional metaplots, as opposed to global metaplots.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T16:58:17-07:00","id":981801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/979378-help-me-decide-to-play-requiem-instead-of-masquerade?p=981791#post981791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I think CoD 2e does have a metaplot, but its mostly unique regional metaplots, as opposed to global metaplots.</div> </div> </div> </div>It has regional settings with lore, backgrounds, and characters. That's not the same thing as a metaplot.<br /> <br /> According to Wikipedia, a metaplot is the overarching storyline that binds together events in the official continuity of a published role-playing game campaign setting. Major official story events that change the world, or simply move important non-player characters from one place to another, are part of the metaplot for a game.<br /> <br /> Since the Chronicles' local settings don't have any events that occur in them after year 0, there is no official continuity, and no worldstate changes; therefore they have no metaplot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T18:28:58-07:00","id":981879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/979378-help-me-decide-to-play-requiem-instead-of-masquerade?p=981791#post981791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If your concidering Tokyo, you might benifit from Changeling the lost 2e, you actually learn about the wider domains in Honsu abit, not just Tokyo, as well as a couple of Changelings who are very involved in Vampire politics. One is the Changelings Ambassador/Envoy to Vampires, an interesting Character, the other is an Ambassador/Envoy to humanity, including a human lead Corporation that is a major power in Tokyo Vampire politics.<br /> <br /> But one thing I would do is add some Jiang Shi to Osaka, just because I find the Jiang Shi interesting, why leave out a interesting, if rare clan.<br /> <br /> I think CoD 2e does have a metaplot, but its mostly unique regional metaplots, as opposed to global metaplots.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am setting my game in Seattle, but there will be Jiang Shi, the Demon Seattle book, and all the 2e books I can afford. Changeling is high on the list.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T22:06:43-07:00","id":981961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/979378-help-me-decide-to-play-requiem-instead-of-masquerade?p=979897#post979897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I were to sum up the requiem clan's identities in one word each, they would be<br /> <br /> Deva: Passion<br /> Gangrel: Instinct<br /> Mekhet: Knowledge<br /> Nosferatu: Fear<br /> Ventrue: Power</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> And if we're going to divide up the Requiem covenant identities, this is how they seem to compare to Masquerade.<br /> <br /> <br /> Invictus: Camarilla (they flat out confirm they're descended from it)<br /> <br /> Carthians: Anarchs (if they ever got their shit together)<br /> <br /> Unaligned: Anarchs (still disorganized and unruly)<br /> <br /> Belial's Brood: Sabbat (except even more psychotic!)<br /> <br /> The rest of the covenants can be used as allegories for independent clans","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T23:34:04-07:00","id":981987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/979378-help-me-decide-to-play-requiem-instead-of-masquerade?p=981961#post981961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And if we're going to divide up the Requiem covenant identities, this is how they seem to compare to Masquerade.<br /> <br /> <br /> Invictus: Camarilla (they flat out confirm they're descended from it)<br /> <br /> Carthians: Anarchs (if they ever got their shit together)<br /> <br /> Unaligned: Anarchs (still disorganized and unruly)<br /> <br /> Belial's Brood: Sabbat (except even more psychotic!)<br /> <br /> The rest of the covenants can be used as allegories for independent clans</div> </div> </div> </div>Its worth noting that the Camarilla the Invictus are descended from bears very little resemblance to the Camarilla of Masquerade beyond the name. That said, if you want to draw equivalences to the Masquerade Sects like that, the Invictus are the closest analogue to the Camarilla as the self-styled Masquerade police, and the Carthians are the closest analogue to the Anarchs as the radical libertarian counterpoint to the Invictus's oppressive political institution. The Sabbat got its themes divided up among several other Covenants, with the Lancea et Sanctum getting their twisted Christian overtones, the Circle of the Crone getting their philosophy of embracing their own Beasts, and Belial's Brood getting their blackhat kill-on-sight status. The Ordo Dracul kind of took up the Tremere's place as the weird occult society that is ostensibly allied with the protagonist Domains, but definitely has their own hidden agenda, and picked up a lot of the weird abilities from various independent Clans as Scales.<br /> <br /> Personally, my favorite political structure to use in Requiem, though it may be a little cliche, is fairly inspired by Masquerade's Sect war structure. I have the First and Second estates (the Invictus and the Lancea et Sanctum) are the two branches of an antidisestablishmentarian institution called the New Camarilla, which enforces the Traditions as law. The Ordo Dracul are an open secret society that officially abides by the Traditions of the New Camarilla, but operates under its own esoteric tennents within New Camarilla Domains. In some Domains, they hold the real power and use the New Camarilla as puppets, while in others they simply maintain small academic circles and hold little to no sway within the Court. The Carthians are a group of separatists that respect the ideas behind the Traditions, but reject the New Camarilla as a governing entity. Carthian Domains generally maintain an uneasy peace with New Camarilla Domains, and large Domains often have both factions coexisting in relative nonhostility, though tensions do occasionally reach a head. The Circle of the Crone are considered heretical by the Lancea et Sanctum and by extension the New Camarilla. Accordingly, the practice of Cruac and the worship of the Crone are outlawed in New Camarilla Domains, though how much this is enforced varies from one Domain to the next. Some Acolytes practice in secret within New Camarilla Domains, but most adherents prefer either to live in Carthian Domains, or to form their own, wherein the Traditions are seen more as personal responsibilities than as legal tennents. The former has the benefit of being considerably safer from Lancea et Sanctum crusaders, while the latter affords them complete political freedom. <br /> <br /> I'm waiting on Secrets of the Covenants before I settle on where Belial's Brood fits into this schema, but I'm hoping they will work similarly to Forsaken's Balehounds in 2E - a secret Covenant of devil worshippers that infiltrate the other Covenants. I could see Sanctified who take the whole cursed by God thing as license to turn to the Devil, Acolytes who worship demons rather than pagan gods, Invictus who sign Blood Oaths to infernal Regnants, Dragons who take their &quot;spit in the face of God&quot; thing a bit too far... Carthians are a little harder to come up with how they would go Brood, but maybe something like taking Paradise Lost as a source of inspiration in too literal a sense, or maybe those that believe Carthian Law has a demonic source... Anyway, you get the idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 10-05-2016, 09:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T00:10:05-07:00","id":981994,"title":"","content":"One thing I like is the flexibility of mixing and matching covenants to generate different kinds of power structures and leadership philosophies. Or throwing in new covenants (although I'm hesitant to do so at this time).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T05:36:53-07:00","id":982076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/979378-help-me-decide-to-play-requiem-instead-of-masquerade?p=981987#post981987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Carthians are a little harder to come up with how they would go Brood, but maybe something like taking Paradise Lost as a source of inspiration in too literal a sense, or maybe those that believe Carthian Law has a demonic source... Anyway, you get the idea.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh, that's easy. Just style them after the Serpent of Eden.<br /> <br /> Tempting the young, naive kindred with promises of power and knowledge so they might stand equally with their elder masters.<br /> <br /> Once their masters find out what they did, they are outraged, which the Brood spins to their advantage by demonstrating the elders don't want them standing up for themselves. This tempts more Carthians to lend an ear to Brood operatives either out of desperation or spite, thus allowing the Brood to spread its corruption.<br /> <br /> <br /> Should I be worried about how easily I can think up a convincing scheme for the evil factions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T06:19:51-07:00","id":982090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/979378-help-me-decide-to-play-requiem-instead-of-masquerade?p=981994#post981994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing I like is the flexibility of mixing and matching covenants to generate different kinds of power structures and leadership philosophies. Or throwing in new covenants (although I'm hesitant to do so at this time).</div> </div> </div> </div>That is one of the strong points of Requiem, for sure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T11:14:23-07:00","id":982215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/979378-help-me-decide-to-play-requiem-instead-of-masquerade?p=982090#post982090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That is one of the strong points of Requiem, for sure.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your post definitely highlighted it, too. I like your basic power structure, as it's very illustrative of the possibilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T16:37:59-07:00","id":982432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/979378-help-me-decide-to-play-requiem-instead-of-masquerade?p=981994#post981994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing I like is the flexibility of mixing and matching covenants to generate different kinds of power structures and leadership philosophies. Or throwing in new covenants (although I'm hesitant to do so at this time).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There's a Cruac ritual that allows you to create Gargoyles, but they operate differently from Masquerade.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Gargoyle_(VTR)\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem Gargoyles</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 10-05-2016, 07:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T17:31:45-07:00","id":982458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/979378-help-me-decide-to-play-requiem-instead-of-masquerade?p=979902#post979902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For one thing, there's no progenitor myth and no generations curse. Your vampire's power levels increases with age and experience, and likewise decreases from long periods of torpor. Generally 50 years in torpor decreases blood potency by 1 point.<br /> <br /> This means that Kindred society in requiem is equal opportunity. The most powerful vampires are the ones who stay active, while those who attempt to sleep through the ages suffer a decrease in their capabilities. If the Antedeluvians tried to pull a doomsday stunt in Requiem, they'd find themselves as weak as Fledglings after sleeping for a few thousand years. And it would probably take centuries for them to even recover an ounce of their lost power.</div> </div> </div> </div>Another cool thing about Torpor in Requiem 2E is that it's the best way for Elder's to remain mental spry. Age too much without Torpor and you get stuck in your ways, a living relic. So without Torpor you remain powerful but can't interact with the mortal world, you have to trade some Vampiric power for the human ability to reinvent yourself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3326-an-fhuiseog","name":"An Fhuiseog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3326_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T19:54:29-07:00","id":982520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>An Fhuiseog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/979378-help-me-decide-to-play-requiem-instead-of-masquerade?p=982458#post982458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another cool thing about Torpor in Requiem 2E is that it's the best way for Elder's to remain mental spry. Age too much without Torpor and you get stuck in your ways, a living relic. So without Torpor you remain powerful but can't interact with the mortal world, you have to trade some Vampiric power for the human ability to reinvent yourself.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I have to agree on Torpor in 2e Requiem being way cooler than Masquerade. In Masquerade Torpor was how ancients would set plots in motion without risking themselves, and in 2e Requiem Torpor was how the vampiric mind refreshed itself and prepared the vampire to be a better vampire, such as in one part of the 2e book it mentions how an Elder vampire who recently awakened was showing another Kindred how to use Twitter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T23:01:26-07:00","id":982563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/979378-help-me-decide-to-play-requiem-instead-of-masquerade?p=982520#post982520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I have to agree on Torpor in 2e Requiem being way cooler than Masquerade. In Masquerade Torpor was how ancients would set plots in motion without risking themselves, and in 2e Requiem Torpor was how the vampiric mind refreshed itself and prepared the vampire to be a better vampire, such as in one part of the 2e book it mentions how an Elder vampire who recently awakened was showing another Kindred how to use Twitter.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> And with that, I now imagine there's a Daeva bloodline who figured out how to channel Majesty through the electronics.<br /> <br /> Don't lie... you know they've tried it!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T23:29:57-07:00","id":982570,"title":"","content":"I like that torpor is not an inherently <i>bad</i> thing but it's also not an inherently <i>required</i> thing. Elders who haven't gone to torpor should be at least somewhat scary with their blood pools in addition to potential traits, devotions, etc. Clearly there's a balance between power and adaptability, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T14:36:02-07:00","id":982937,"title":"","content":"Oh so! I am thinking of starting my Requiem game in the 70s or 80s, and I came across <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/60377/New-Wave-Requiem?\" target=\"_blank\">New Wave Requiem, which is pretty inexpensive on OBS</a>. Anyone have any impressions of this?<br /> <br /> I grew up in the 80s, which may help a bit. I also think that starting a few decades back provides some leeway to advance the timeline as appropriate without worrying too much about the immediate or near actual future.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T14:45:48-07:00","id":982939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/979378-help-me-decide-to-play-requiem-instead-of-masquerade?p=982937#post982937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh so! I am thinking of starting my Requiem game in the 70s or 80s, and I came across <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/60377/New-Wave-Requiem?\" target=\"_blank\">New Wave Requiem, which is pretty inexpensive on OBS</a>. Anyone have any impressions of this?<br /> <br /> I grew up in the 80s, which may help a bit. I also think that starting a few decades back provides some leeway to advance the timeline as appropriate without worrying too much about the immediate or near actual future.</div> </div> </div> </div>Makes sense. Also, depending on the age of the PCs at &quot;start&quot;, you might be able to roll in Flashbacks, if necessary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T14:49:36-07:00","id":982942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/979378-help-me-decide-to-play-requiem-instead-of-masquerade?p=982939#post982939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Makes sense. Also, depending on the age of the PCs at &quot;start&quot;, you might be able to roll in Flashbacks, if necessary.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I imagine there will be flashbacks going back to the 50s and 60s.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T14:57:02-07:00","id":982944,"title":"","content":"I love New Wave Requiem so much. For a long time I used the cover as my profile picture here. It's largely a setting book, light on mechanics so it's super easy to port to 2e and well worth the price.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T15:02:27-07:00","id":982950,"title":"","content":"Excellent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T07:53:37-07:00","id":983320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/979378-help-me-decide-to-play-requiem-instead-of-masquerade?p=982937#post982937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh so! I am thinking of starting my Requiem game in the 70s or 80s, and I came across <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/60377/New-Wave-Requiem?\" target=\"_blank\">New Wave Requiem, which is pretty inexpensive on OBS</a>. Anyone have any impressions of this?<br /> <br /> I grew up in the 80s, which may help a bit. I also think that starting a few decades back provides some leeway to advance the timeline as appropriate without worrying too much about the immediate or near actual future.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> 80's Daeva... have fun with that! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T14:46:29-07:00","id":983542,"title":"","content":"Totally going to have fun with that!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T14:53:23-07:00","id":984070,"title":"","content":"So I am thinking that my Seattle will be dealing with Carthian - Invictus tensions as Carthians are in charge and Invictus are jockeying for everything they can get before they bring the whole thing down. There is a prince, but he's part of a ruling council, rather than a singular despot. Representatives on the council would include more than one covenant, but with the majority being Carthians. Still deciding whether there's elections (and if so there's probably only been one or two) and how the kindred feel about that. Carthian rule is fairly recent relative to the starting date (1976), having started in the 1960s.<br /> <br /> There's also Lancea et Sanctum - Circle tensions, and I want both covenants to be relatively evenly matched and definitely prone to conflict. I haven't put a lot of thought into this as yet.<br /> <br /> Nothing special decided about the Ordo Dracul. I have a couple of members outlined, but I'm not sure what to do with them.<br /> <br /> I am tempted to add Tremere is a sixth Covenant, but that depends on how cleanly thaumaturgy translates into Requiem.<br /> <br /> And I realize both of the conflicts I've described are pretty typical. I'm just trying to find ways to rearrange them slightly rather than coming up with something new.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T15:27:31-07:00","id":984086,"title":"","content":"Ooh, a Carthian city! Those are fun. The thing I like to play up with the Carthians is that when they're in power, they're their own worst enemies. They're a great way to showcase why tearing down the system without having a plan for what to replace it with doesn't work. Might be cool if the tensions with the Invictus are actually a source of stability for the Carthians, giving them a reason to present a united face, when they would otherwise fall to infighting.<br /> <br /> The thing about the Ordo Dracul is that they often don't much care who holds political power in the city, as long as they're allowed to conduct their research in peace (or able to conduct it in secret, either way works). They might support the Carthians if they think the inefficiency will work as a distraction while they stick a giant bendy straw in the biggest nexus of weird energy they can find. If you're crossing over with Splintered City at all, I'm sure they would be fascinated by the time shards.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T15:58:42-07:00","id":984102,"title":"","content":"Yes, to Splintered City. I can see why both the Ordo Dracul and House Tremere would be interested in operating there, if they have some way to interact with the splinters. Which they probably do, and it would make the God-Machine a factor in the game, if not actual angels and demons.<br /> <br /> And yes to the Invictus creating stability by giving Carthians a reason to present a united front. I am thinking there are probably 2-3 Carthian factions based on what they think the ideal government would be, and that's going to be a source of internal strife. The one probably in the least favor would be the communists, given that this is starting at the height of the Cold War. Not that vampires are necessarily patriots but that kindred society can mirror human society. Like in New Wave, the kindred have their own urban legends of Satanic rituals going on Belial's Brood supposedly abducting and embracing children, for example, plus suspicions about the Circle of the Crone being connected to Belial's Brood, for example. Except in this case it's communists. I think I also want an anarchist faction, and I haven't worked out what number three will be, except that their star is ascendant and the prince is from that faction. The other two scheme and plot while presenting solidarity against the Invictus.<br /> <br /> One thing about Seattle that I have an impression of is that it is a fairly pagan and pagan-friendly city. I mean not that everyone or even most people are pagan, but that there are a lot of pagans and a lot of events, and I want to tie the Circle of the Crone to that, although I don't think paganism in the Seattle area becomes big until the 80s. Paganism was definitely a thing, though. The Covenant of the Goddess formed in 1975, for example, although that was in California. I mean, I am pretty sure that most pagans would be horrified by the stuff the Circle does, but I also imagine the Circle would maintain mortal ties with the pagan community, eventually.<br /> <br /> I don't want a Lancea et Sanctum as unsympathetic as Solomon Birch's take on the thing in the fiction. I mean I want it to be harsh but not to the point of nailing kindred to swastikas. One thing I do want is a kind of rift between the LeS and Invictus due to perceived lack of support when the Carthians took over. They're more like co-belligerents than allies, and the LeS is certainly trying to lean on the council to get what they want when such things come up.<br /> <br /> I am thinking there's probably 10 council members total, and half of them are Carthians. Probably a couple Invictus, two from the LeS, and one from the Circle of the Crone. Not aiming for quotas so much just considering. As long as things remain in the political arena, the Carthians have the advantage, but there are quite a few kindred unhappy with Carthian rule and that's definitely going to be a thing.<br /> <br /> There are ~1,900,000 people in the greater Seattle area in the mid-70s, and ~500,000 people living in Seattle proper. I'm not sure what suggested vampire demographics are. With 1:50,000 that's 38 vampires in the greater Seattle area, which is possibly quite sufficient.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T16:40:01-07:00","id":984112,"title":"","content":"So if I do have the Tremere, I need to come up with some history and motivations.<br /> <br /> One recommendation I like in the conversion guide is to make the Tremere both a covenant and a bloodline, offering either Auspex or Dominate as a fourth discipline, and thaumaturgy being a third form of blood magic, but hopefully adaptable with the Blood Sorcery book. The bloodline also allowing members of any clan to join (there's apparently some precedent for this?).<br /> <br /> So Thaumaturgy would have paths (Blood, Lure of Flames, Movement of the Mind, etc) as well as rituals. This would eat up a lot of experiences for anyone trying to master them all, so I imagine most Tremere would have 1-2 paths. I was thinking paths would cost 4 experiences per dot, and rituals would cost 2 experiences - basically the same as Cruac or Theban Sorcery. I considered having a favored path like a favored coil but it seemed like Thaumaturgy should be priced more like the other blood sorceries.<br /> <br /> As far as what the Tremere's history is, I don't know yet. I know there are Tremere in Mage: The Awakening (I have the first edition Vampire, Werewolf, Mage, and WoD books) and that embracing an awakened mage just doesn't work. Are there equivalents to hedge mages in CofD? Like people who use more limited magic and aren't awakened?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T16:46:33-07:00","id":984113,"title":"","content":"One possibility is that House Tremere was formed by blood sorcerers looking for a way to standardize their work. Possibly blood sorcerers who were formerly members of other covenants. There's probably some friction because of this, although they would have split off a few centuries before.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T23:35:23-07:00","id":984279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/979378-help-me-decide-to-play-requiem-instead-of-masquerade?p=984112#post984112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So if I do have the Tremere, I need to come up with some history and motivations.<br /> <br /> One recommendation I like in the conversion guide is to make the Tremere both a covenant and a bloodline, offering either Auspex or Dominate as a fourth discipline, and thaumaturgy being a third form of blood magic, but hopefully adaptable with the Blood Sorcery book. The bloodline also allowing members of any clan to join (there's apparently some precedent for this?).</div> </div> </div> </div>There is precedent for Bloodlines available to any Clan. They're highly atypical, but they do exist, and what are the Tremere if not atypical?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/979378-help-me-decide-to-play-requiem-instead-of-masquerade?p=984112#post984112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So Thaumaturgy would have paths (Blood, Lure of Flames, Movement of the Mind, etc) as well as rituals. This would eat up a lot of experiences for anyone trying to master them all, so I imagine most Tremere would have 1-2 paths. I was thinking paths would cost 4 experiences per dot, and rituals would cost 2 experiences - basically the same as Cruac or Theban Sorcery. I considered having a favored path like a favored coil but it seemed like Thaumaturgy should be priced more like the other blood sorceries.</div> </div> </div> </div>You've got to check out Sacriments and Blasphemies. It breaks Sorcery Disciplines into five separate Themes, each with a purview, and allows you to improvise rituals using these Themes. In my opinion, the best way to handle Thaumaturgy in Requiem would be to use Themes as Paths. Basically, where other Blood Sorcery Disciplines are restricted to using prepackaged Rituals, Thaumaturges can learn Paths/Themes that allow them to cast creatively. That's how I'd do it, anyway<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/979378-help-me-decide-to-play-requiem-instead-of-masquerade?p=984112#post984112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As far as what the Tremere's history is, I don't know yet. I know there are Tremere in Mage: The Awakening (I have the first edition Vampire, Werewolf, Mage, and WoD books) and that embracing an awakened mage just doesn't work. Are there equivalents to hedge mages in CofD? Like people who use more limited magic and aren't awakened?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Tremere in Awakening are a Legacy of Liches - one of the lagest Left-Handed Legacies, big enough that they are practically an Order. They do have a historical connection to a group of Vampires, though in modern times they are generally regular Mages who join the Legacy. Probably not quite what you're looking for here, but if you're curious check out Left-Handed Path for more details on them. There are a few types of non-Mage magic users in Chronicles. Proximi are kid of Awakening's version of Hedge Mages, humans with very limited access to Supernal magic. There are also a lot of human-only supernatural Merits, which can be used to make pretty effective non-Awakened sorcerers. If you want to go that route, there has been a preview of Secrets of the Covenants that shows off an Ordo Dracul Mystery with a Coil focused on gaining supernatural Merits in spite of the usual human-only restrictions. You could make the Tremere a faction of the Ordo Dracul as opposed to a Covenant of their own. They could have exclusive knowledge of said Coil, and membership in their Mystery could be the prerequisite for joining their Bloodline, which could grant Thaumaturgy as a fourth Discipline, which could just be the only way to access Themes from Blood Sorcery. That's how I would do it, anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T04:26:38-07:00","id":984347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/979378-help-me-decide-to-play-requiem-instead-of-masquerade?p=984279#post984279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is precedent for Bloodlines available to any Clan. They're highly atypical, but they do exist, and what are the Tremere if not atypical?</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly!<br /> <br /> I might drop the bloodline idea. I got it from the conversion guide, and it does seem like an interesting idea, but it makes the Tremere very exceptional relative to other bloodlines and covenants.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/979378-help-me-decide-to-play-requiem-instead-of-masquerade?p=984279#post984279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You've got to check out Sacriments and Blasphemies. It breaks Sorcery Disciplines into five separate Themes, each with a purview, and allows you to improvise rituals using these Themes. In my opinion, the best way to handle Thaumaturgy in Requiem would be to use Themes as Paths. Basically, where other Blood Sorcery Disciplines are restricted to using prepackaged Rituals, Thaumaturges can learn Paths/Themes that allow them to cast creatively. That's how I'd do it, anyway</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll definitely check it out, just haven't gotten to it yet.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/979378-help-me-decide-to-play-requiem-instead-of-masquerade?p=984279#post984279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Tremere in Awakening are a Legacy of Liches - one of the lagest Left-Handed Legacies, big enough that they are practically an Order. They do have a historical connection to a group of Vampires, though in modern times they are generally regular Mages who join the Legacy. Probably not quite what you're looking for here, but if you're curious check out Left-Handed Path for more details on them. There are a few types of non-Mage magic users in Chronicles. Proximi are kid of Awakening's version of Hedge Mages, humans with very limited access to Supernal magic. There are also a lot of human-only supernatural Merits, which can be used to make pretty effective non-Awakened sorcerers. If you want to go that route, there has been a preview of Secrets of the Covenants that shows off an Ordo Dracul Mystery with a Coil focused on gaining supernatural Merits in spite of the usual human-only restrictions. You could make the Tremere a faction of the Ordo Dracul as opposed to a Covenant of their own. They could have exclusive knowledge of said Coil, and membership in their Mystery could be the prerequisite for joining their Bloodline, which could grant Thaumaturgy as a fourth Discipline, which could just be the only way to access Themes from Blood Sorcery. That's how I would do it, anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah, I meant to say I was basically going to ignore the Mage Tremere, acknowledging they exist but that's it. I might have them actually exist in the game I am going to run, which could I suppose provide for an interesting mystery.<br /> <br /> As far as mortal hedge magic I let that go because I wanted the Tremere to be a synthesis of existing blood sorcery practices, rather than a mage order gone horribly wrong. I feel like I'd have to buy a lot of books to be able to do the mortal stuff justice.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure about making the Tremere a faction in the Ordo Dracul. If I do then they're going to dominate the Ordo in Seattle. I also see them as having more political aspirations than the Ordo Dracul, looking at their various powers as things to parley into power in kindred society. I mean that's what they'll be like separate from the Ordo, but your suggestion is appealing. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I am hesitant to make blood sorcery or Thaumaturgy bloodline disciplines, though.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T08:54:17-07:00","id":984442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/979378-help-me-decide-to-play-requiem-instead-of-masquerade?p=984102#post984102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haven't worked out what number three will be, except that their star is ascendant and the prince is from that faction.</div> </div> </div> </div>What about &quot;Democracy, Fuck Yeah!!!&quot; (the 3 exclaimation points are deliberate). Make them a pastiche over every over-the-top Eagle-land trope you can think of. If the Prince has a ghoul familiar, it's probably a bald eagle. That kind of thing. You already said there is voting, so some form of Democracy or Republic seems to be in effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T08:59:36-07:00","id":984445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/979378-help-me-decide-to-play-requiem-instead-of-masquerade?p=984113#post984113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One possibility is that House Tremere was formed by blood sorcerers looking for a way to standardize their work. Possibly blood sorcerers who were formerly members of other covenants. There's probably some friction because of this, although they would have split off a few centuries before.</div> </div> </div> </div>What about them originating as a group of vampires that either worked with Mages (perhaps even Tremeres) or enslaved a group with Blood Bonds. Excessive, near exclusive, feeding on Mage Vitae, and experimentation into just how Mages work their magic leads to the Covenant's Blood Sorcery, and the Bloodline's formation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T10:32:16-07:00","id":984486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/979378-help-me-decide-to-play-requiem-instead-of-masquerade?p=984347#post984347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Exactly!<br /> <br /> I might drop the bloodline idea. I got it from the conversion guide, and it does seem like an interesting idea, but it makes the Tremere very exceptional relative to other bloodlines and covenants.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well in the New World of Darkness (or at least the Mage setting), the Tremere vampires are mentioned to have existed at some point, but they're now extinct. I would imagine any chronicle involving them would take place in the Dark Ages when they're still kicking around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 10-09-2016, 01:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T11:41:08-07:00","id":984528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/979378-help-me-decide-to-play-requiem-instead-of-masquerade?p=984486#post984486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Well in the New World of Darkness (or at least the Mage setting), the Tremere vampires are mentioned to have existed at some point, but they're now extinct. I would imagine any chronicle involving them would take place in the Dark Ages when they're still kicking around.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mentioned them to say I wasn't using them, so their history is irrelevant to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T11:51:29-07:00","id":984532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/979378-help-me-decide-to-play-requiem-instead-of-masquerade?p=984442#post984442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What about &quot;Democracy, Fuck Yeah!!!&quot; (the 3 exclaimation points are deliberate). Make them a pastiche over every over-the-top Eagle-land trope you can think of. If the Prince has a ghoul familiar, it's probably a bald eagle. That kind of thing. You already said there is voting, so some form of Democracy or Republic seems to be in effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know what this means. I mean the dominant Carthian faction is all about democracy, but they're not so much all about the US as it exists.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/979378-help-me-decide-to-play-requiem-instead-of-masquerade?p=984445#post984445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What about them originating as a group of vampires that either worked with Mages (perhaps even Tremeres) or enslaved a group with Blood Bonds. Excessive, near exclusive, feeding on Mage Vitae, and experimentation into just how Mages work their magic leads to the Covenant's Blood Sorcery, and the Bloodline's formation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I want an origin that doesn't draw directly on Mage, I think, but I do appreciate the advice. I'll think it over. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2367,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","user":"Resplendent Fire","date":". 10-09-2016, 02:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T11:51:42-07:00","id":984533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/979378-help-me-decide-to-play-requiem-instead-of-masquerade?p=984486#post984486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Well in the New World of Darkness (or at least the Mage setting), the Tremere vampires are mentioned to have existed at some point, but they're now extinct. I would imagine any chronicle involving them would take place in the Dark Ages when they're still kicking around.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or you could find one in Torpor, trapped where they couldn't wake up on their own. Maybe paved over or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T12:29:30-07:00","id":984550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/979378-help-me-decide-to-play-requiem-instead-of-masquerade?p=984532#post984532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know what this means. I mean the dominant Carthian faction is all about democracy, but they're not so much all about the US as it exists.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, you could always pull from the older Democratic sources, if you want. I just figured US City, Voting/Democracy, why not use the tropes?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/979378-help-me-decide-to-play-requiem-instead-of-masquerade?p=984532#post984532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want an origin that doesn't draw directly on Mage, I think, but I do appreciate the advice. I'll think it over. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Do you not want to have to use or reference Mage material in game, or you don't want Mages to exist in the setting at all?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T12:55:05-07:00","id":984560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/979378-help-me-decide-to-play-requiem-instead-of-masquerade?p=984550#post984550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, you could always pull from the older Democratic sources, if you want. I just figured US City, Voting/Democracy, why not use the tropes?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, fair enough. I am going for the whole &quot;Carthians as revolutionary&quot; thing and there's definitely some disappointment in the US with both Watergate and Vietnam in recent memory.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/979378-help-me-decide-to-play-requiem-instead-of-masquerade?p=984550#post984550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you not want to have to use or reference Mage material in game, or you don't want Mages to exist in the setting at all?</div> </div> </div> </div>I am going to use and reference Mage material in game. I'm using some of the advice for the Tremere in the conversion guide but I want the Tremere to probably have an origin separate from Mage. I guess it depends on whether I pick up Left Hand Path and what I think of the stuff on the Tremere in there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T14:59:12-07:00","id":984608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/979378-help-me-decide-to-play-requiem-instead-of-masquerade?p=984442#post984442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What about &quot;Democracy, Fuck Yeah!!!&quot; (the 3 exclaimation points are deliberate). Make them a pastiche over every over-the-top Eagle-land trope you can think of. If the Prince has a ghoul familiar, it's probably a bald eagle. That kind of thing. You already said there is voting, so some form of Democracy or Republic seems to be in effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>I find it difficult to imagine that appearing in a domain where Invictus as I know them calls the shots, but I would imagine that sort to appear in these two scenarios:<br /> <br /> 1. Carthians vs. Old World extremely 1e Invictus<br /> This is where Invictus were seen as aristocratic, European toffs and they don't even pretend to offer opportunity to ambitious newcomers. I wouldn't expect that to happen Seattle, but maybe it could work.<br /> <br /> 2. Carthians vs. McCarthians<br /> So this is where they form in opposition to a distinctly undemocratic and un-American (in no-true-Scotsman terms) faction of Carthians, communists being the obvious choice.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/979378-help-me-decide-to-play-requiem-instead-of-masquerade?p=984347#post984347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not sure about making the Tremere a faction in the Ordo Dracul. If I do then they're going to dominate the Ordo in Seattle. I also see them as having more political aspirations than the Ordo Dracul, looking at their various powers as things to parley into power in kindred society. I mean that's what they'll be like separate from the Ordo, but your suggestion is appealing. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>This is why I see Tremere as Invictus. They make their through Masquerade by making themselves an indispensable pillar of the Camarilla and while they are <i>the</i> occult clan (of the Camarilla) they don't seem to have a mystical endgame in mind, besides perhaps outlasting other vampires","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","user":"Spencer from The Hills","date":". 10-09-2016, 06:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T15:25:32-07:00","id":984619,"title":"","content":"So to elaborate on why I don't want to connect the Tremere covenant (or subgroup within Ordo Dracul if I go that way) is basically that embraced mages die. I know something different happened with the Tremere vampires in Mage but I feel like the whole thing opens cans of worms I don't really want to deal with in a predominantly vampire game. So, the Tremere from Mage won't exist, but their existence wouldn't be relevant to the game I want to run anyway. If I decide I want to do liches I'll probably call them something else.<br /> <br /> I am totally going to crossover, though, although to what extent I'm not sure. I love the idea of Ordo Dracul investigating the splinters (Demon) in Seattle, so that's probably going to be a thing. I also have some ideas for Werewolf and Mage. I'm going to pick up other 2e corebooks as I can and incorporate what I can when I can. But the primary focus will be on vampires and I don't really want any vampire stuff to directly depend on other game lines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T05:03:00-07:00","id":984825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/979378-help-me-decide-to-play-requiem-instead-of-masquerade?p=984619#post984619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So to elaborate on why I don't want to connect the Tremere covenant (or subgroup within Ordo Dracul if I go that way) is basically that embraced mages die. I know something different happened with the Tremere vampires in Mage but I feel like the whole thing opens cans of worms I don't really want to deal with in a predominantly vampire game. So, the Tremere from Mage won't exist, but their existence wouldn't be relevant to the game I want to run anyway. If I decide I want to do liches I'll probably call them something else.<br /> <br /> I am totally going to crossover, though, although to what extent I'm not sure. I love the idea of Ordo Dracul investigating the splinters (Demon) in Seattle, so that's probably going to be a thing. I also have some ideas for Werewolf and Mage. I'm going to pick up other 2e corebooks as I can and incorporate what I can when I can. But the primary focus will be on vampires and I don't really want any vampire stuff to directly depend on other game lines.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Fair enough. I was just thinking, the Mage connection would make greater crossover sense, and yet be utterly irrelevant in modern nights - at this point, <i>where</i> Clan/House/Bloodline/Covenant Tremere got their mojo is academic. And probably subject to lies and/or distortions.<br /> <br /> Of course, there are <i>so many</i> magical traditions and sources in the CofD. You could also just make Tremere vampires into magic pirates, by which I mean they steal/appropriate any and all magical techniques they can get their hands on. Thaumaturgy? Pilfered. Spirit Rites? Adapted. Etc. All of that lore distilled down into their own brand of Blood Sorcery. Kinda like the Ordo Dracul, but where the Dragons focus on self-improvement and new discovery, Tremere focuses on external sources and old lore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T05:25:30-07:00","id":984831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/979378-help-me-decide-to-play-requiem-instead-of-masquerade?p=984825#post984825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fair enough. I was just thinking, the Mage connection would make greater crossover sense, and yet be utterly irrelevant in modern nights - at this point, <i>where</i> Clan/House/Bloodline/Covenant Tremere got their mojo is academic. And probably subject to lies and/or distortions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that makes sense, and now you've given me the idea to have like three different stories about how Tremere got their mojo.<br /> <br /> I feel like I'm ending up putting a lot of effort into something that I just thought would be cool to include. I worry about it becoming a pet covenant or overdoing them in relation to other covenants.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/979378-help-me-decide-to-play-requiem-instead-of-masquerade?p=984825#post984825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course, there are <i>so many</i> magical traditions and sources in the CofD. You could also just make Tremere vampires into magic pirates, by which I mean they steal/appropriate any and all magical techniques they can get their hands on. Thaumaturgy? Pilfered. Spirit Rites? Adapted. Etc. All of that lore distilled down into their own brand of Blood Sorcery. Kinda like the Ordo Dracul, but where the Dragons focus on self-improvement and new discovery, Tremere focuses on external sources and old lore.</div> </div> </div> </div>Magic pirates is not far off from where I was going, although I was thinking primarily of them getting their stuff by adapting Theban Sorcery and Cruac. Having them seek out other sources of magical lore makes a lot of sense and is consistent with what I envisioned initially. This also gives them their own unique flavor. Thanks much for the suggestion. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T14:12:06-07:00","id":985061,"title":"","content":"And it looks like this thread has run its course, so:<br /> <br /> Thank you to everyone who answered. You've given me a lot to think about in terms of running Requiem, and showed me a lot about the game that I didn't pick up on my own reading. Going to have a lot of fun with this. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T14:18:17-07:00","id":985063,"title":"","content":"Books on my reading list based on recommendations. Hoping I didn't miss anything.<br /> <br /> Vampire: The Requeim Second Edition*<br /> God-Machine Chronicle* (probably going to get Chronicles of Darkness in hardcopy, though)<br /> Splintered Seattle (+Demon)<br /> Damnation City*<br /> New Wave Requiem*<br /> Blood Sorcery*<br /> Danse Macabre<br /> Clanbooks<br /> Covenant books<br /> <br /> * is purchased. The rest have to wait a bit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T14:48:56-07:00","id":985084,"title":"","content":"Oops. I bought Blood Sorcery last year and forgot about it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> So that's another one down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T14:11:41-07:00","id":985665,"title":"","content":"Get those Clan books ASAP, they're fantastic. Covenant books are alright as well, though to shoe them into the 2ed framework takes a little finnagling. That or wait for Secrets of the Covenants to come out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2291-gwyn-chan-r-gwyll","name":"Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T14:37:40-07:00","id":985682,"title":"","content":"Clanbooks are gonna be October. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Definitely on the list, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T05:47:29-07:00","id":986072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/979378-help-me-decide-to-play-requiem-instead-of-masquerade?p=985682#post985682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Clanbooks are gonna be October. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Definitely on the list, though.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Good news and bad news...<br /> <br /> <br /> Bad News - Nosferatu don't have Schrecknet in Requiem.<br /> <br /> <br /> Good News - They can <i>literally</i> scare people to death.<br /> <br /> <br /> Worse News - The Noctuku (slight name change) are a bloodline of Nosferatu cannibals who devour the flesh of other vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 10-12-2016, 08:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T05:55:23-07:00","id":986076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/979378-help-me-decide-to-play-requiem-instead-of-masquerade?p=986072#post986072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Good news and bad news...<br /> <br /> <br /> Bad News - Nosferatu don't have Schrecknet in Requiem.<br /> <br /> <br /> Good News - They can <i>literally</i> scare people to death.<br /> <br /> <br /> Worse News - The Noctuku (slight name change) are a bloodline of Nosferatu cannibals who devour the flesh of other vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>I love the Requiem take on Nosferatu. Esp. that their bane doesn't require them to look monstrous, just that they're disturbing even if they look relatively &quot;normal.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T09:48:17-07:00","id":986190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/979378-help-me-decide-to-play-requiem-instead-of-masquerade?p=984279#post984279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is precedent for Bloodlines available to any Clan. They're highly atypical, but they do exist, and what are the Tremere if not atypical?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Which come to think of it, the Morbus should be one such bloodline. Their condition sounds like something that could be adopted by any kindred, similar to Malkavia. And there are many different ways the Lancea, Dragons, and Circle could make use of the power to control disease.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T09:55:51-07:00","id":986193,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/979378-help-me-decide-to-play-requiem-instead-of-masquerade?p=986190#post986190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which come to think of it, the Morbus should be one such bloodline. Their condition sounds like something that could be adopted by any kindred, similar to Malkavia. And there are many different ways the Lancea, Dragons, and Circle could make use of the power to control disease.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, I like it as a Mekhet Bloodline. The thing is, Morbus was never a disease in and of itself, vampires of the Bloodline just became careiers of other diseases. You can't even call it an immunodeficiency decease, because vampires don't have working immune systems in the first place. Morbus has never been something you can catch.<br /> <br /> I don't know, we'll see what they do with it when Dark Eras Companion comes out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T10:11:18-07:00","id":986201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/979378-help-me-decide-to-play-requiem-instead-of-masquerade?p=986193#post986193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh, I like it as a Mekhet Bloodline. The thing is, Morbus was never a disease in and of itself, vampires of the Bloodline just became careiers of other diseases. You can't even call it an immunodeficiency decease, because vampires don't have working immune systems in the first place. Morbus has never been something you can catch.<br /> <br /> I don't know, we'll see what they do with it when Dark Eras Companion comes out.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Well I was more referring to the idea of them only being able to draw sustenance from contaminated blood, which certainly sounds like some kind of mystical infection going on behind the scenes. Remember that not every bloodline is produced from a conscious act of will, some can be brought into existence through curses. What if at some point in the past, a coterie or something was cursed to feed exclusively on the ailing, and the curse was passed onto their descendants?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T10:39:36-07:00","id":986214,"title":"","content":"We know when the Morbus Bloodline originated, it was in Rome during the rule of the Camarilla, it was probably more of a curse than a conscious act of will, and it was not contagious. It had to be willingly passed on, just like every other Bloodline.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T12:35:14-07:00","id":986304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/979378-help-me-decide-to-play-requiem-instead-of-masquerade?p=986214#post986214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We know when the Morbus Bloodline originated, it was in Rome during the rule of the Camarilla, it was probably more of a curse than a conscious act of will, and it was not contagious. It had to be willingly passed on, just like every other Bloodline.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> That's just speculation. The book says that even the Morbus don't know their own origins. Rome is just the earliest they can trace their lineage. And even then, their supposed founder wasn't the one who invented the power over disease, he learned while traveling with the crusades.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T23:07:13-07:00","id":986599,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2367_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2367\" data-vbnamecard=\"2367\">Resplendent Fire</a> , few years back I got idea on making Tremere secret/urban legend faction inside Ordo Dracul. Think of them as Illuminati in Order of Dragon. They build hidden hierarchy by Blood Bonds and in comparison to normal Dragons, want to steal magic of other supernaturals for their occult blood powers, instead on only learning Coils to superpass vampirism. They probably started as small Covenant centureis ago ( maybe Fall of Rome ), but infiltrated Ordo with them as Vlad Tepes started his group, plotting to overcome Order from inside. Tremere Bloodline where probably starting point of the group. I hope it helps in making both Tremere and Ordo Dracul more interesting. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 10-13-2016, 03:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T23:10:54-07:00","id":986600,"title":"","content":"Thanks - those are some interesting ideas you have there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-18T21:30:47-08:00","id":1005233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wissenschaft</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/979378-help-me-decide-to-play-requiem-instead-of-masquerade?p=979887#post979887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why not just make your Brujah prince Deva? The clans are flexible enough in Requiem that going against stereotype is easy and fun. Deva don't have to be the seducer. I only say this because they share the same initial discipline spread. Not sure if that matters.<br /> <br /> Also, I would strongly recommend the covenant books. Especially the Invictus book because its a great insight into vampire high society. It gives a lot of neat ideas on how to set up the prince's court (if they happen to be Invictus).</div> </div> </div> </div>The adjective I'd use for the Daeva is &quot;passionate&quot;, which is the same one I'll use for the Brujah, yeah, you can rarely go wrong by translating your Brujah characters into Daeva.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}